$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Acety5-(4-methylpyridin-3-yl)-2,3-dihydro-1 H-indole (23). The title
compound was synthesized according to method A using 17a (150 mg, 0.52
mmol), 3-bromo-4-methylpyridine (70 μL, 0.63 mmol), sodium carbonate (277
mg, 2.61 mmol), and tetrakis- (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (30 mg, 0.
03 mmol) in dimethoxyethane (9 mL) and water (3 mL). The crude product
was purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (MeOH/CH2Cl2, 0
to 2%) and crystallization from acetone. Pale yellow crystals, yield 85
mg, 65%. mp 180 −182 °C. Rf = 0.50 (MeOH/CH2Cl2 1:20). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 2.25 (s, 3H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 3.26 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 4.12 (t,
J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.12 −7.18 (m, 3H), 8.27 (d, J = 8.2 Hz,1H), 8.41 (m,
2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 19.9, 24.1, 28.0, 48.9, 116.7, 125.2,
125.3, 128.8, 131.5, 133.1, 137.6, 142.5, 144.8, 147.8, 149.7, 168.8. MS
(ESI) m/z = 253 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Pyridyl- or Isoquinolinyl-Substituted Indolines and Indoles as
Potent and Selective Aldosterone Synthase Inhibitors
