$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.2. Ethyl
4-(2-Bromophenyl)-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (4a) (Typical
Procedure; See Table 1, Entry 1). Ethyl
4-bromo-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (2b) (310 mg, 1 mmol),
K2CO3 (279 mg, 2 equiv), Pd(dppf)Cl2 3DCM (41 mg, 0.05 mmol), and
2-bromophenylboronic acid (264 mg, 1.8 mmol) were dissolved in
dioxane/H2O (3:1) (2 mL). The stirred mixture was heated to reflux
(preheated oil bath) and refluxed for 2 h until the reaction was finished
(TLC), before it was allowed to cool to ca. 20 °C. It was diluted (DCM,
20 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and adsorbed onto silica gel. Dry flash
chromatography (hexane/t-BuOMe, 4:1) gave the title compound 4a (378 mg,
98%) as colorless cubes, Ethyl
3-(2-Chloropyrid-3-yl)-6-methoxy-1,5-naphthyridine-3-carboxylate (4k).
(220 mg, 64%) as colorless cubes. mp 120-122 °C (pentane), Rf 0.77
(t-BuOMe); (found: C, 59.4; H, 4.1; N, 12.3. C17H14ClN3O3 requires C,
59.4; H, 4.1; N, 12.2); λmax (DCM)/nm 232 (log ε 3.69), 263 (3.07), 328
(3.01), 338 (3.00); νmax/cm-1 3044w, 2986w, 2945w, 2907w, 1722s (C=O),
1611 m, 1572w, 1557w, 1495s, 1479w, 1449w, 1429w, 1395s, 1371w, 1341 m,
1281 m, 1261 m, 1234s, 1215 m, 1179w, 1146w, 1115 m, 1074w, 1015 m, 974w,
851 m, 810 m, 773 m; δH (500 MHz; CD2Cl2) 9.38 (1H, s, Ar H), 8.50 (1H,
br s, Ar H), 8.32 (1H, d, J = 9.0, Ar H), 7.66 (1H, d, J = 7.4 Ar H),
7.437.41 (1H, m, Ar H), 7.24 (1H, d, J = 9.2, Ar H), 4.244.22 (2H, m,
OCH2), 3.74 (3H, s, OCH3), 1.13 (3H, t, J = 7.0, CH3); δC (125 MHz;
CD2Cl2); 165.6 (s), 162.9 (s), 149.8 (s), 149.0 (d), 148.6 (d), 144.5
(s), 143.9 (s), 140.4 (d), 139.8 (s), 139.7 (d), 133.1 (s), 125.9 (s),
122.0 (d), 118.8 (d), 62.0 (OCH2), 54.1 (OCH3), 14.0 (CH3); m/z (EI) 309
(MH+ -Cl, 19%), 308 (M+ -Cl, 100), 298 (3), 280 (69), 252 (7), 237 (4),
227 (4), 220 (3), 206 (4), 192 (5), 165 (6), 138 (3), 126 (2), 114 (2),
100 (2), 87 (2).
