$DATUM N,N’-Bis(1-hexylheptyl)-2,5,8,11-tetra(3-pyridyl)perylene-3,4:9,10-tetracarboxylic
acid bisimide (5c): A mixture of 2b (50.4 mg, 40.1 μmol), Pd2dba3•CHCl3
(8.5 mg, 8.20 μmol), K2CO3 (51.7 mg, 375 μmol), SPhos (6.60 mg, 16.1
μmol), and 3-iodopyridine (166 mg, 810 μmol) in 5 mL of toluene/H2O (4/1)
was stirred under nitrogen at 105 °C for 17 h. After the reaction, H2O
was added and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layers
were washed with brine and dried over Na2SO4. The mixture was purified by
silica gel column chromatography with CH2Cl2/MeOH as eluent. After
recrystallization from CH2Cl2/MeOH, compound 5c was obtained in 64% yield
(27.4 mg, 25.8 μmol). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 0.83 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 12H),
1.21–1.24 (m, 32H), 1.63–1.68 (m, 4H), 1.97–2.03 (m, 4H), 4.90 (tt, J =
6.0, 9.6 Hz, 2H), 7.46 (dd, J = 5.0, 8.0 Hz, 4H), 7.78 (dt, J = 2.0, 8.0
Hz, 4H), 8.39 (s, 4H), 8.68 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 4H), and 8.74 (dd, J = 2.0,
5.0 Hz, 4H) ppm. 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 14.06, 22.55, 26.86, 29.10, 31.76,
31.88, 55.03, 76.45, 76.64, 123.13, 125.89, 127.61, 131.14, 132.68,
135.31, 137.82, 148.36, and 149.07 ppm; UV/vis (CH2Cl2): λ max = 460,
491, and 528 nm. Fluorescence (CH2Cl2, λ ex = 450 nm): λ em = 540 nm;
HR-MS (ESI-MS): m/z = 1097.5492, calcd for (C70H74ClN6O4)+ = 1097.5466
([M + Cl]+).
