$DATUM Boronate ester 10: A mixture of TBS ether S9 (764 mg, 1.95 mmol),
bis(pinacolate)diboron (743 mg, 2.93 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (22.0 mg, 0.098
mmol) and KOAc (574 mg) in DMF (7.0 mL) was heated at 80 °C. After
stirring for 3h, the reaction was quenched with H2O and extracted with
ethyl acetate. The organic layer was washed with H2O and brine, dried
over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on SiO2 (ethyl acetate/hexane 1:100 to 1:50).
Dioxaborolate 10 (491 mg, 64%) as a colorless amorphous 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.35 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 5.96 (s,
2H), 4.96 (s, 2H), 1.33 (s, 12H), 0.9 (s, 9H), 0.06 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.80, 146.51, 130.74, 127.94, 107.59, 100.90, 83.51,
59.07, 26.17, 25.00, 18.70, -4.97; HRMS (ESI, M+Na) calcd for
C20H33BNaO5Si 415.2088, found 415.2082.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Origin of Stereocontrol in Guanidine-Bisurea Bifunctional Organocatalyst
That Promotes α-Hydroxylation of Tetralone-Derived β-Ketoesters:
